Unity Examples – Access to Variables, Methods, Game Objects and ScriptsYou can search for game objects with certain tags using GameObject.FindWithTag and GameObject.FindGameObjectsWithTag. 
Use GameObject.Find to find a game object by name.
using UnityEngine;
using System.Collections;

public class example : MonoBehaviour {
	void Start() {
		GameObject go = GameObject.Find("SomeGuy");
		go.transform.Translate(0, 1, 0);
		GameObject player = GameObject.FindWithTag("Player");
		player.transform.Translate(0, 1, 0);
	}
}
 From <https://docs.unity3d.com/410/Documentation/ScriptReference/index.Accessing_Other_Game_Objects.html>

Unity Examples – Access to Variables, Methods, Game Objects and ScriptsYou can use GetComponent on the result to get to any script or component on the found (another) game object
The <> reference a component of the type specified…
using UnityEngine;
using System.Collections;
 
public class example : MonoBehaviour {
	void Start() {
		GameObject go = GameObject.Find("SomeGuy");
		go.GetComponent<OtherScript>().DoSomething();
		GameObject player = GameObject.FindWithTag("Player");
		player.GetComponent<OtherScript>().DoSomething();
}
}

